{
  "name": "camels",
  "description": "Revenge of the Mutant Camels (Jeff Minter / Llamasoft, 1984), C64. This is the DECRUNCHED RUNTIME IMAGE - the program as it exists in memory after the loader on \"revenge of the mutant camels.d64\" has finished - so addresses here are live addresses, not file offsets.\n\nThe map, as worked out by amber, beryl and basalt:\n  $0800-$0FFF  spriteBank: the 32 sprites of the current zone, copied here by CopySpriteSet\n  $1000/$1800/$4000/$4800  the four sprite sets it copies from\n  $1D00-$1FFF  object system: 16 slots, positions, speeds, types, plus the sprite multiplexer\n  $2000-$27FF  the character set (VMCSB is written once, $8AE7 STA #$18: screen $0400, chars $2000)\n  $5000-$5847  front end: title, options, high scores, pause, cheat banner\n  $5870-$58FF  leftover assembler source, not game data\n  $5900/$5980  two-voice jingle\n  $5A00-$5DFF  attract-mode scroll text (the credits)\n  $5E00-$5ECF  high score table, loaded from and saved to \"ATTACK MUTANT.HI\"\n  $5F00/$5F80  the two player status-line slots (more source residue underneath)\n  $6000-$66F5  three-voice intro tune, plus one stream nothing plays\n  $6240-$62FF  animated character frames\n  $6700-$87CF  THE ZONE TABLE: 42 records of 200 bytes, banner at +$A0 of each\n  $87FE-$9FEE  the game itself\n  $A000-$BFFF  not the program - BASIC ROM shows through here and $8D1D reads it as a random source\n  $C000-$C11E  loader stub, high-score load/save, KERNAL restore\n\nA custom character set means punctuation is not standard screen codes: $51=. $52=, $53=apostrophe $54=! $55=? $56=: . The derivation is a comment at $56AE.\n\nThe cheat code is GOATS ($96D2).",
